<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-attractor`>>

!! The Pono Roadmap ~ the attractor reads STABLE FOUNDING

''STABLE FOUNDING'' names the state the house grows toward (operator-ruled). Once a Lararium stands, its
base state reads STABLE: a PRIVATE household SEED (its own charter, one seat) for the operator's own devices, and a FOUNDED PERSONA
ZERO. Everything else flows downstream of it — contracting into other Nexuses and founding a Nexus with a second operator, inviting the operator's own
PersonaGroup devices, and hosting guests who walk.

''The first rung reads the memory-stage hearth'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-31, #/rulings). Before any rung above it, one operator's node and browser stand joined on one machine, each from its anon floor through the full rites: the operator's hand performs the founding, the unlock, the browser passphrase and the join acts, and a harness walks the same rites through the test door (#/cold-start). A page edit reaches the worn face's daemon working top, `<projections>/wikis/daemon-<F>`, and the CLI and the MCP seat read and write that same wiki. The house's own design tracking and its self-improvement loops then move off untracked scratch files onto that wiki, a memory stage (#/stride-0-hearth). The rung stands up the working Lararium the live-test rulings ask for first (#/rulings, a working Lararium comes first), and every rung above it inherits the walk it proves.

This carrier holds the house's ONE roadmap, and ONLY what binds or stays owed. A cold session that
reads the boot seed and then this carrier can pick up any thread: the instruments and the law that bites
(#/cold-start), the order a free slot takes (#/the-order), the rulings (#/rulings), the design decisions that shape unbuilt work (#/decisions),
the six paths in one order (#/the-road), every open item in the stride that holds it (#/the-loops indexes the strides),
each train's commits in order (#/the-trains), the lanes that run beside the road (#/side-lanes), the fresh
start (#/fresh-start), and what the operator owns (#/open). Landed work reads in git and the
CHANGELOG, never here. No count rests here: each reading names the instrument that takes it. Law lives in
its own carrier, and this carrier points there.

''Full models land early'' (operator ruling; quote license: //"Full caps now … Full models in early, so we don't code churn later."//). The road takes no staging by milestone: a slice builds its whole model, with its whole capability reach, in the place the order gives it, and no slice ships a narrower interim that a later slice must re-cut.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-order`>>

!! The order ~ every open item ranked into waves (reprioritized 2026-11-16)

''The frame'' (operator, 2026-11-16: //"NO BACK COMPAT. At the merge, the code should read as if it has always been this way, we shall export the existing ~/.lares wikis & bas and re-import into the brand-new house as QA proof before the PR merges."// and //"Talk out what on the roadmap meme we have accomplished recently (true it up), and what sits to do immediately next"//). The dogfood hearth stands re-founded and worn: the steward's daemon wiki holds the house laws, the rulings, the open ledger, the standing orders and where things live, the wake reads that index at every session start, `works` stands minted, and sessions dogfood from inside the Lararium through the MCP seat and the CLI. The worn house (`L45` to `L48`, #/the-leaps) stands on the span of PR #218. The table ranks every open item of this carrier, the leaps of #/the-leaps and the items of every stride alike, into four bands: AT THE MERGE (the span closes, and the operator's house carries into a brand-new one as the merge's proof), RIGHT AFTER (the edges the span's cold reads named), WAVE TWO (beside the dogfooding), and AFTER. A free slot takes the lowest open rank whose files no flying lane holds. The owner law of #/the-road still names one hand per compose hunk, and four lanes fly at most under the lane law (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff#/the-lane-law`>>); the lanes in flight and their heads rest in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff#/state`>>.

''The rank law'' (the house's reading, overrulable): first what blocks the operator's re-founding and dogfooding; then what breaks a rule the operator stated; then what unlocks the most later items; then cost. Each rank carries one sentence of reason. The keeper rite keeps every qualification its rulings name (#/rulings, 2026-11-07, the dogfood/keeper split): its gates rank in AFTER, and no dogfood re-founding waives one.

|! Rank |! Band |! Items |! Reason |
| 2 | AT THE MERGE | the aftermath sweeps, no back-compat: the retired names out of canon, the tool and test pins of retired shapes, narration by package, canon history, "records, not rows" and the class-5 identifiers, then the CHANGELOG and every evergreen ceiling at its final count (loops `Y1` to `Y6`; plans in the controller's scratch, rulings at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/ruling/2026-11-16`); Y5b's lanes B and C of the name table (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/y5b-name-table) stand landed and lane A (custody) builds; bytes at rest and keys on the wire (the domain string `"sealed-index-row"`, the JSON key `rows` in the promotion ledger, the carry manifest and the `wiki_filter` answer, the `row` field on refusal classes) keep their spelling through Y5b and reopen after the merge as their own slice, with a re-bake; beside them the carry-parity witness (`tools/carry-parity.mjs`, red first: it names a deleted meme, a changed one and a dropped share) | The merged code reads as though it always stood this way, and the carry proof needs an instrument that can fail before any house crosses. |
| 2a | AT THE MERGE, ahead of rank 3 | the backup caps, so the Lararium holds every writer the backup repo takes (the order and both plans at lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/cross-and-keep; the keep's design at lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/evergreen-keep): `K1` `keep-cut` wakes each cold wiki in turn, hands the operator's pins back and refuses by name per (face, slug) on a shut face, so a page put into a cold wiki travels in the cut (`packages/lares-cli/src/rite-keep.ts`, `commands/rite.ts`, `tools/keep-cold.test.mjs`); `K2` the keep cuts house-only content, a workbench whose mirror rests beside the canon source staying out and the manifest naming it under `elsewhere` (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/carry.ts`, `packages/lararium-node/src/carry-manifest.ts`); `K11` the keep carries the device's AI-session state: `bin/sync`'s pieces move into `lares rite keep` (the device id and its refusal on a foreign `DEVICE.json`, the mirror of the `~/.claude` config, plugins, state and each project's `memory/`, the secret scan with its planted fixtures), all under `devices/<name>-<id8>/` in the same commit and the same push as `house/` (`packages/lares-cli/src/rite-keep-host.ts`, a new `keep-sessions.ts`, `keep-config.ts`); the cadence covers `down`, an explicit `lares rite keep` and a session-end hook running `lares rite keep --if-due`, each push spending one return of the keep lei, which the operator sizes (the unlock offers twelve, and the wake names the count left); `bin/sync` retires once `K11` reads par against one real sync, and the repo's README names a Lararium as its writer | The re-bake's image carries whatever code stands at the re-bake, so with the caps in it the founded house's first `down` keeps the whole house and the device's sessions with no second image; every push into the backup repo rides a keep lei the operator strung, one writer per working tree, authority by capability and never by an ambient SSH key. |
| 3 | AT THE MERGE | the rehearsals and the bake: the walker's carry leg under the scoped rehearsal exception (an image at the live house's revision seeds and exports, an image at the span's head imports, parity reads par; the leg wakes each wiki in turn before the export, wearing each face that wrote there, and the source export's `cold-wikis` and `override-bases-unread` over woken wikis read as named, lossless for records, a cold wiki's working rows travelling without their override bases (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/ruling/2026-11-16); the leg and its seed burn after the lit house, rank 4e), one clean walker pass on the final head, then one labelled genesis re-bake (the operator's approval, once the caps of rank 2a and CI stand green) | The real house crosses only a road a scratch house walked first, and the image the operator stands carries the final floor. |
| 3a | AT THE MERGE | the house keeps itself (operator, 2026-11-16: //"build it into the house's machina … allow the operator's unlock password to drive the whole thing through the lei caps system"//; plan lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/house-backup): the house writes a cleartext, importable carry bundle into an operator-named workspace mirroring a private repo, under a lei the operator's unlock strings; the carry rite keeps the source house's last cut there before the founded house stands. BUILT: `lares rite keep` (its vessel half `rite keep-cut`) lays the bundle into `house/` of the workspace (`house/** -text` in the clone's `.gitattributes`), spends one return of a keep lei the operator strings by hand or by a yes at `vault unlock`, scans for secret-shaped strings, commits, pushes and lands the tessera; `--if-due` keeps only a house that moved, the shim's `down` makes that call, and the wake prints the keep line (`LARES_KEEP_WORKSPACE`, or the one `LARES_WORKSPACES` pair, names the workspace). WAITING: the operator's env line at the lit house, a live keep on the founded house, and before the merge the cold-wiki cure (`K1`), the house-only cut (`K2`) and the device's sessions (`K11`) at rank 2a, with `K5` the root cure after the merge (rank 13c); the keep's standing design rests at lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/evergreen-keep. The rite's name stays `keep`: `waiho` names the nihomano binding sigil | The house's memory rests on one disk until it does; the carry rite and the iris/pūlama re-founding both lean on a cut that survives the tear-down. |
