''The rite's ledger and the day's handbacks'' (2026-11-13):
* The confirm gate rides `C4`, the shared Kahu-cabal workbench for house-canon wikis rides `P21` (#/the-leaps, the leaps of 2026-11-14).
* ''A draft's recovery mirror shares one path across faces'' (`<projections>/wikis/<slug>/recovery`): each face's unsaved drafts of a shared wiki rest in the one folder, and the export carries them under no face.
* ''The fifth rehearsal's residue'' (2026-11-14): an export names no omission where a shared workbench's folder carries zero pages (a reader's hold alone wakes no working mirror; the runbook's carry block holds as a seated writer first); the final seed's zero line; the handoff walk's `kahua_list` read per face; a wrong passphrase at the browser reset shows no error line (`C4`); `--base ""`.
* ''A contract-tier bag never rides the public floor.'' The public floor every DreamNet user reads by CID carries `public`-tier bags alone, read off each bag's own `meta.mem` at the genesis bake and at each release cut (a bag that declares no tier reads `veil` and stays off); the contract-tier `bags/elyncia-referee` keys no snapshot, and a hearth founded earlier sheds its referee snapshot at its next `lares nexus release <file> --cut`, the slug named in `dropped`. Owed under that law: the referee recipe that mounts `elyncia-referee` for a contracted seat.
* ''One resolver answers house canon.'' `resolveHouseCanon` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/house-canon-doc.ts`) answers every door that reaches house canon: the Kahu realm's standing document first (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/offering#/the-canon-offer`>>), a registry entry only where the realm names none. A house-canon wiki the realm names no document for mints none, files no catalog entry and keys its slot bindings on `floorCanonAddress` (`floor:<bag>`). Owed: burning a stale `bags/lares` catalog entry an earlier boot filed.
* ''The console door's remainder'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/browser-vessel-lift#/the-console-door`>>): a verb plane, where each verb declares a `console` surface and the door projects the daemon's reads by that declaration; `vault lock` house-wide (the browser refuses it `locks-by-leaving`, and a lock that closes every tab's session needs a locked state on the page and a road to unlock on a standing connection); the build revision read off the arrival descriptor into `vessel read`.
* ''A crossing leaves no log line at the face gate'' (`face-gate-server.ts` writes none): one line per admitted and per refused crossing, naming the face and no key material; the wire's own silence stays (#/decisions, silence, one deadline).

''Items with wake conditions'': the herm-never-unlocks refusal, before a herm stands for real; the signed local channel (`F11`) covering `meme_put`, before a second human, a remote seat or a non-operator process writes the hearth; the parallel-drafts door, when a second place joins a face; `lares vessel read --control` (a read-only, redacted view of control records), the daemon document's vessel state moving into the control document, and a page-dispatched verb's answer travelling back to its page island.

''After the walk'' (#/the-order ranks each): the Mu on the two floor confirmations (#/rulings, 2026-11-10; rank 28); the control-plane leap, `bags/daemon` moving to the vessel's control home (rank 34); the branch burn by reachability from `main`, the race sampler branches among them (rank 38); the complete re-think of the multi-model and swarm procedures once the Lararium fully stands (#/rulings, 2026-11-13; rank 31). The AI's memory frame and the kahua two-tier lift ride `L35`; `M5`'s memory migration, rulings and feedback first, rides rank 4; the span's pull request to `main`, then `develop`, rides rank 2.

