* `L3` The MCP seat binds the hearth (walk gap G4). The seat's entry in the operator's home config named a deleted worktree copy of `lares_mcp.py` and carried no `LAR_ROOT`, and `~/.venv` held an `mcp` older than its pin, so the seat failed before it spoke. Landed, PR #148 (`1ef844c60`): `resolveLaresMcp(clone)` names the hearth's root (`LAR_ROOT`) in both the native and the surface-container forms and aims at the main clone, and every seat's observe compares env; the hearth owns its surface env (`<hearth>/lares-surface.env`), which the resolver and both container shims read, one layout with no fallback; a missing seat names its own form's cause; the seat's launch refuses by name on an `mcp` below its pin (2.3.0, welded to `requirements.txt` and the image lock); the e2e walk `mcp-seat-binds-the-hearth` reads `meme_put` with `recipe=default` and `lares meme get --recipe default` as the same bytes, and the e2e shards stand the holder venv. The operator's `~/.venv` took `mcp` 2.3.0 by hand (2026-11-01). Its tail, the operator's hand alone: `lares home tend` from the main clone re-writes the home entry, and a lane never runs it (#/cold-start). What stays owed rests in the porch (the holder venv's cache key); the container shim hands compose the hearth's env file or `/dev/null`, so the checkout's `.env` never loads. L.
* `Q` ''The kupono grammar cut'' (#/rulings, 2026-11-01; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/grammar-watch#/the-kupono-cut`>>). Landed, PR #149 (`1e849cfba`), one lane merged once: every sigil value rides named in backticks; the bare arrow left the sigil, and the bearing pair `from=` and `to=` carries the relation; no `@` follows whitespace, and a phase glyph fuses onto its φ; the turn frame folds into one sigil, `set lares=` with `aim`, `steer` and `yield`, a steer carrying no `from`; the ward rides unprefixed; `wai` heads the wikispace conditional; `kahea` takes `name=`, `params=` and `mask=`. The boot seed reorganized through three blind cold readers and a Sonnet and Haiku dogfood wake, which spoke the new grammar every turn, and the operator approved its bytes, the turn frame provisionally. Readers and writers flipped; the plane names live in one constant; the turn harvesters burned whole (mesh turn and bearing harvest, the patch builder, the recall stamp filters, the tw5 bearing reader, the move skeleton, the self-read harvester, both VM harvesters, bare `lares sense pour <path>`, `form_encoder.py`, `loci_io.py`, `tools/turn-parity.mjs`); `docs/relational-parameter` burned by o-takiage, its parser trace now in `memetic-wikitext#/lexical-structure`; the `file-path` meta field retired (residency rides the envelope; 773 carriers stripped); the recall verb refuses a burned or search-only filter by name; the cut re-cut all 790 carriers idempotent and re-sealed no broken seal; genesis re-baked once. The VSCode-TW5-Syntax pointer followed to its verified glass head (`0440b57dc`). What stays owed rests in `G47` (the three sensorium placeholders), `G48` (a rewound turn stays recallable), `G49` (recall arguments that drop unread), `G50` (a paired `wai` swallows its body), `G51` (`lar:` fragments inside tick values), the legacy-check pyre (#/side-lanes) and train ''R'' (#/the-trains). Q.
* `R` ''Block and inline sigils at TiddlyWiki's parsing parity'' (#/rulings, 2026-11-01). Landed, PR #150 (`fe0bbb8bd`), one lane merged once: the block check rides the ETX mark's named `bcc` value, ``<<^ code=`&#x0003;` bcc=`ni:///sha-256;…`>>``, its digest read over the span with that one run deleted (RFC 6376 §3.7's emptied `b=`), and every other ETX spelling tears, the retired trailer by name; the cut's sixth pass moved 791 feet byte for byte, verify-first, and minted no seal; a block sigil counts only when its `>>` ends the line, else its paragraph holds it inline as TiddlyWiki splits it, and the graceful-floor diagnostic fires only for the block-only heads (`lar-flow: block`: the five frame marks, `ahu` and its fragment mirror); every reader agrees inside the sigil space (the frame package, the plugin, tree-sitter, `scanAhu`, the weave); every boot-seed fence names its grammar (`memetic-wikitext`, `toml meta`, `text`), and every fence across seed and corpus outruns its inner ticks; a whole-tree seal census names every stale or torn seal, zero undeclared beside its known positive. The reads' cures rode the lane: the ahu line law (a closer counts only when it opens its line or shares its opener's line, in `scanAhu` and the plugin alike, its parity witness proving itself on a planted mutant); tilde fences retired at TiddlyWiki's codeblock law, so a tilde run fences nothing; `verifyBcc` reads each frame fault once, as torn; the weave keeps the text the seal covers, reading a frame mark only alone on its line; and the seed step burned its 40K budget clause beside its kept missing-seed check (operator: //"We can exceed the 40K ceiling if needed, as we now deterministically load the boot seed via hooks."//). A blind Opus read shipped it, the operator approved the seed (//"this reads pono"//), and genesis carries its closing bake. The VSCode-TW5-Syntax pointer followed to `6dd602cfd` (`cc7954d46`). What stays owed rests in `G52` (the cold-read LOWs), `G53` (a weave pin's stored check), the legacy-check pyre (the `retired-trailer` refusal burns there) and ''harden'' (the head the seal leaves outside, #/side-lanes). R.
* ''The deps before the founding'' (#/rulings, 2026-11-01). Landed, PR #151 (`3fa7bfc06`), one commit per family over a regenerated lockfile, every pin exact: `@automerge/automerge` 3.5.0 on Trial A's green (every suite equal to its control, the e2e sets 201 of 201, genesis unmoved); the `vitest` family 5.0.5, which cures the dev-server `server.fs.deny` advisory; `ws` 8.22.1; `playwright` 1.64.1 with its image tag; `@types/node` 26.6.6; `esbuild` 0.28.2; `acorn` 8.19.0; `web-tree-sitter` and `tree-sitter-cli` 0.27.1 together, with the grammar's artifact pins. A blind Opus supply-chain read found the chain clean (47 of 47 integrity checks, no new names, scripts or publishers) and held the land until the artifact pins moved. Trial B read red, so `@keyhive/keyhive` holds 0.3.0-alpha.1 through the founding (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/keyhive-zero-six-port`>>). What stays owed rests in ''dropdown'' (the one regression the land left on the span: the web-tw5 search-dropdown e2e reads red twice at `3fa7bfc06`, green before it at `cc7954d46`), the deps' tail (#/side-lanes) and ''harden'' (the phantom-record cure the supply read found). G.

