!! The trains ~ each train's commits in order, what it waits on, and its riskiest step

''Rules every train keeps'': every commit leaves HEAD building, and a fix or batch boundary leaves its unit
suites green; red first, with a control, the red its own commit; `tools/typecheck-witness.sh` in every
battery; one e2e file locally and the whole sets on CI; one push per batch; a scratch root and a
scratch `HOME` for anything that writes custody. A step marked ''live'' changes a shape the
wire or a signature carries.

''The solo chain.'' Each of these holds the compose hunk in `open-node-vessel.ts` and
`open-browser-vessel.ts` while it runs, and no other node lane lands beside it: S, then K's seat, flip,
rename, scopes and founding act, then N's sealing and self-contracts, then W's three live steps, then W's
dials, then E, then O1's sessions through its switch, then H's hosting act through its strangers' dial, then X.
T's stage-cut (`T12`) joins the chain as one named single-owner step after `T6`'s pins: for its window every other
lane stops at module boundaries.

!!! L ~ the memory-stage hearth (leads the road; waits on nothing above it; items in #/stride-0-hearth)
# The walk's small items rest in #/ashes and #/o-takiage (`L1` to `L3`, `L5` to `L7`); `L3`'s tail stays the operator's `lares home tend`.
# `F11`'s signed channel and Mask, before any second hand writes the operator's own hearth, and `L22`'s `S4` to `S6`, after the standing.
# `L4p` with `L4f`, the stage walk's proof: a joined page's edit on disk, read back by the CLI and the MCP seat, and a CLI write shown in the page; then `L17`, the seat's filter, render and act verbs.
# The operator's hand: the fresh start on one machine, the founding, the unlock, the passphrase slot, the join acts, `lares home tend`.
# The stage: `L8`'s law in its carrier first, then `L10` to `L12` on the stage's own tools.
# `L18` the narration fence, `L19` with `L21` the memory o-takiage and its batch lift, and `L13`, the move, the rung's acceptance; `L14`, the promotion verb, last; `L20`, the fiction and art domains, after the move.
''Gate'': `L4p` and `L17` open on a stood hearth (the hearth stood on 2026-11-13, and the tiddler door stands; #/the-order, rank 3), and `L8` to `L13` follow `L4p`.
''Riskiest'': the join on the operator's own hearth, a human-run walk of the full rites; a wedge there costs a fresh start by hand, which the single-operator re-found ruling prices at nothing git cannot restore.

!!! T ~ the test re-cut (beside every path; items in #/stride-t-recut; kit <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/test-recut-road`>>)
# ''Landed ahead'': `T1`, the Stryker probe (#/o-takiage).
# ''Ruling now on this train'': red-first, homed. A fix lands a behavior red and control in the narrowest existing home; a new file opens only at a distinct runtime, boundary, harness or suite class.
# ''Luna fold-ins on this train'' (2026-11-04): the Luna growth read measured rapid test growth with most new case lines landing in new files, and the procedure read (the Luna procedure read, 2026-11-04) set the home law that keeps new cases in existing homes unless a boundary demands a new file.
# Wave 0, the cures, each red-first: `T19`, `T20`, `T22`, `T27` and `T33` to `T35` rest in #/o-takiage; `T21` and `T23` to `T26` follow as slots free; `T37` the keyslot's owed hygiene in a custody slot; `T28` rides `W30`; `T29` beside `T4`'s sweep.
# Wave A, parallel and composer-free: `T3` rests in #/o-takiage and `T2`'s fixture stands; `T2`'s codemod, `T36` the founded-custody template and `T38` the canon-law lane stand open; `T4` the dead-export sweep (one announced batch right after a controller land), `T5` the pure readers (after `ralias`, which stands).
# Wave B: `T6` the boot's characterization pins, `T7` the flake families' events, `T8` the test-only export census, `T30` the layer map, `T31` the corpus scans' budget, `T32` node's slowest files.
# Wave C, after `T6` and `u1`: `T10` boot cells, `T11` the share inputs, `T12` the stage-cut in its window, `T13` the shared cap-stack stages one per PR, `T14` the verb math, `T15` the mirror witness, `T16` injected homes, `T17` injected deadlines, `T18` mutation as an inspection list (`T9`'s process-global doors burned with `promote`, #/ashes).
''Riskiest'': `T12`, a cut of the boot composer that every lane composes through; `T6`'s pins and the single-owner window answer it.

!!! S ~ the custody seal (SUBSTRATE; it stands)
Its state reads in #/the-road's SUBSTRATE block, and nowhere else. The engine fold owes its live image proof (`S2`).

!!! G ~ ground (waits on nothing; rides beside every train on disjoint files)
The GROUND items of #/the-road, tests-only work first. Riskiest: the summons cures, which touch what a verb's effect means.

!!! K ~ R-CHARTER, stage one: the seat (closed)
Its steps stand landed and read in git: the seats sign with their own keys under per-seat cold digests and a threshold, one name serves a Nexus, edges and scopes commit to the Nexus AID, per-Nexus keys mint at random with the signed hand-over, a PersonaGroup founds as a Keyhive group, and the Stable founding act stands a hearth (#/ashes, `K`).
